# What the rust CI image's build may see of the checkout: the one script it
# runs.
#
# The image is built on the published toolchain image and copies one file of
# the checkout, the devcontainer's languages/rust/targets.sh, which adds the
# project's musl target, so the context sent to the builder is that file, and
# nothing else a commit touches is uploaded or busts a layer. A file added to
# the Dockerfile's COPY lines is added here and to the image pipeline's path
# filter.
#
# There is a second reason this file exists. BuildKit reads the ignore file
# named after the Dockerfile in preference to the root .dockerignore, and this
# workspace has a root .dockerignore: an allowlist written for the images under
# deployments/, which re-includes the Rust and web workspaces those builds read.
# Without this file the build of a CI image would upload them for nothing.

*
!/.devcontainer/languages/rust/targets.sh
